# Roles and access control

Canon: `docs/ADVANCED_BUSINESS.md` (actors + capability matrix) · helpers: `src/lib/roles.ts` · edge: `src/proxy.ts` · UI nav: `dashboard-shell.tsx`.

## Capability helpers

- `canManageRequests` → SA | PM — requests, contact-leaks, create/assign/approve-on-behalf, soft-delete/restore
- `canManageUsers` → SA | PM — Admin → Users (list, approve/reject, create/edit, activate)
- `canManageServices` → SA | PM — Admin → Services (catalog, attributes, reorder)
- `canManageFinance` → SA | FM — payments, finance, subscriptions, finance/payment settings
- `canManagePlatform` → SA only — packages, activity, contacts, maintenance
- `canAccessAdminPath(role, path)` — shared by proxy + admin layout

## tRPC procedures (`src/server/trpc.ts`)

| Procedure | Who |
|-----------|-----|
| `adminProcedure` | SUPER_ADMIN |
| `requestManagerProcedure` | SA \| PM |
| `userManagerProcedure` | SA \| PM |
| `servicesManagerProcedure` | SA \| PM |
| `financeManagerProcedure` | SA \| FM |
| `providerProcedure` | PROVIDER \| SA |
| `clientProcedure` | CLIENT \| SA |
| `staffProcedure` | any staff — **unused**; prefer narrower procedures |

## Homes

PM → `/admin/requests` · FM → `/admin/finance` · SA → `/admin` · Provider → `/provider` · Client → `/client`

## Checklist when adding admin UI

1. Gate the **route** in `canAccessAdminPath` if new section.
2. Gate the **procedure** with the correct middleware.
3. Add **nav** entry in `adminNavConfig` with the right `access` tag (`platform` | `users` | `services` | `requests` | `finance` | `settings` | `staff`).
4. Update capability matrix in `docs/ADVANCED_BUSINESS.md` if product scope changes.
